userspace
=========

Pyxplot's data model: the pplObj structure which holds every value, the
types of object and their methods, physical units, dates, and the context
structure which holds the state of a whole session. Several modules split
their header in two: a .h file of types, and a _fns.h file of functions.

context.c, context.h
    The ppl_context structure, which holds the whole state of a session
    (settings, namespaces, evaluation stack, error status, multiplot canvas),
    and the functions which create and free it.

contextVarDef.c, contextVarDef.h
    Looks up variables in the namespaces (built-in, global, and the local
    namespaces of subroutines), including dotted names such as a.b.c.

pplObj.h
    The pplObj structure and the codes of its types (number, string, list,
    dictionary, etc.), and the structures which hold vectors, matrices, files
    and types.

pplObj.c, pplObj_fns.h
    Constructors for each type of object, and functions to copy objects
    shallowly or deeply.

pplObjUnits.h
    The base units (length, time, mass, ...) in which physical dimensions are
    expressed, and the structure describing each unit in the unit database.

pplObjFunc.c, pplObjFunc.h, pplObjFunc_fns.h
    The descriptors of function objects, of each kind (built-in, user-defined,
    subroutines, splines, histograms, Fourier transforms), and functions to
    free and copy them.

pplObjMethods.c, pplObjMethods.h
    The methods of each built-in type, e.g. string.len(), list.sort() and
    matrix.inv(), and the methods common to all objects.

pplObjCmp.c, pplObjCmp.h
    Compares objects, for comparison operators and sorting, and converts colors
    between the RGB, HSB and CMYK color spaces.

pplObjPrint.c, pplObjPrint.h
    Renders objects as text, for print, str() and the display of results.

pplObjDump.c, pplObjDump.h
    Writes objects as Pyxplot expressions which recreate them, for the save
    command and file.dump().

garbageCollector.c, garbageCollector.h, stack.h
    Reference counting: freeing objects when their last reference goes. Also
    the functions which push, pop and resize the stack on which expressions
    are evaluated.

unitsArithmetic.c, unitsArithmetic.h
    Arithmetic on quantities with physical units, including the special
    handling of temperatures in degrees Celsius and Fahrenheit.

unitsDisp.c, unitsDisp.h
    Chooses the units and SI prefixes in which to display a quantity, renders
    numbers with their units, and parses unit names such as "km/s**2".

calendars.c, calendars.h
    Converts between dates and unix times in the Julian, Gregorian, Hebrew and
    Islamic calendars, formats dates as strings, and handles timezones.
